        "fallbackBehavior": "Each per-ilk OSM retains a delayed current value and queues the next value; if its peek is invalid or Spot is not poked, the Vat keeps the prior safety price and can become stale rather than accepting a fresh invalid value.",
        "observedAt": "2026-07-14",
        "collateralParameters": [
          {
            "asset": "Governance-approved Vault collateral ilks",
            "note": "Each ilk has its own Spot liquidation ratio, Vat debt ceiling and floor, Dog liquidation penalty and capacity, and dedicated Clipper auction contract; governance can change these parameters."
          }
        ],
        "liquidationMechanism": "When a Vault becomes unsafe under its ilk's safety-adjusted Spot value, Dog.bark confiscates the position, assigns its debt to Vow, and promptly starts that ilk's Clipper Dutch auction; auction price decreases over time and can be reset under per-ilk parameters.",
        "liquidationDelaySec": 0,
        "backstop": "Collateral-auction proceeds cancel the seized debt; residual system debt is recorded in Vow, can first be netted against protocol surplus, and can become eligible for the documented governance-token debt-auction mechanism after the debt-queue delay.",
        "shutdownOrBadDebtBehavior": "Uncovered liquidation debt remains in Vow's debt queue and can mature into debt-auction-eligible bad debt. Sky's archived End documentation describes system caging and collateral settlement but marks End deprecated, so this profile does not treat emergency shutdown as a currently active guarantee.",
